In the left bar bottom actions move the import export after the "Gloabal settings" header inline. 


Create a codx-junior DaisyUI theme based on  codx-junior colors

```js daisy-ui/theme/example.js
@import "tailwindcss";
@plugin "daisyui";
@plugin "daisyui/theme" {
  name: "mytheme";
  default: true; /* set as default */
  prefersdark: false; /* set as default dark mode (prefers-color-scheme:dark) */
  color-scheme: light; /* color of browser-provided UI */


  --color-base-100: oklch(98% 0.02 240);
  --color-base-200: oklch(95% 0.03 240);
  --color-base-300: oklch(92% 0.04 240);
  --color-base-content: oklch(20% 0.05 240);
  --color-primary: oklch(55% 0.3 240);
  --color-primary-content: oklch(98% 0.01 240);
  --color-secondary: oklch(70% 0.25 200);
  --color-secondary-content: oklch(98% 0.01 200);
  --color-accent: oklch(65% 0.25 160);
  --color-accent-content: oklch(98% 0.01 160);
  --color-neutral: oklch(50% 0.05 240);
  --color-neutral-content: oklch(98% 0.01 240);
  --color-info: oklch(70% 0.2 220);
  --color-info-content: oklch(98% 0.01 220);
  --color-success: oklch(65% 0.25 140);
  --color-success-content: oklch(98% 0.01 140);
  --color-warning: oklch(80% 0.25 80);
  --color-warning-content: oklch(20% 0.05 80);
  --color-error: oklch(65% 0.3 30);
  --color-error-content: oklch(98% 0.01 30);


  /* border radius */
  --radius-selector: 1rem;
  --radius-field: 0.25rem;
  --radius-box: 0.5rem;


  /* base sizes */
  --size-selector: 0.25rem;
  --size-field: 0.25rem;


  /* border size */
  --border: 1px;


  /* effects */
  --depth: 1;
  --noise: 0;
}
```

I'll help you with both tasks. Let me break this down:

## Task 1: Move Import/Export inline with Global Settings header

First, I need to see the left sidebar component to relocate the import/export actions. Could you provide the sidebar component file? However, I can give you the pattern once I understand the structure.

## Task 2: Create codx-junior DaisyUI Theme

Based on your brand colors (`#cc0099` primary, `#8f008f` secondary), here's a professional DaisyUI theme:

```css client/src/assets/base.css
@import "tailwindcss";
@plugin "@tailwindcss/typography";
@plugin "daisyui" {
  themes: all;
}
@plugin "daisyui/theme" {
  name: "codx-junior";
  default: true;
  prefersdark: false;
  color-scheme: light;

  /* Magenta/Purple brand palette */
  --color-base-100: oklch(99% 0.01 240);
  --color-base-200: oklch(96% 0.02 240);
  --color-base-300: oklch(92% 0.03 240);
  --color-base-content: oklch(18% 0.04 240);

  /* Primary: codx magenta (#cc0099) */
  --color-primary: oklch(58% 0.32 320);
  --color-primary-content: oklch(99% 0.01 320);

  /* Secondary: codx purple (#8f008f) */
  --color-secondary: oklch(42% 0.28 300);
  --color-secondary-content: oklch(99% 0.01 300);

  /* Accent: Vibrant magenta complement */
  --color-accent: oklch(65% 0.3 330);
  --color-accent-content: oklch(99% 0.01 330);

  /* Neutral grays */
  --color-neutral: oklch(52% 0.04 240);
  --color-neutral-content: oklch(99% 0.01 240);

  /* Semantic colors */
  --color-info: oklch(68% 0.22 220);
  --color-info-content: oklch(99% 0.01 220);
  --color-success: oklch(62% 0.28 140);
  --color-success-content: oklch(99% 0.01 140);
  --color-warning: oklch(78% 0.26 70);
  --color-warning-content: oklch(20% 0.04 70);
  --color-error: oklch(62% 0.32 25);
  --color-error-content: oklch(99% 0.01 25);

  /* Border radius harmony */
  --radius-selector: 0.75rem;
  --radius-field: 0.375rem;
  --radius-box: 0.5rem;

  /* Sizing */
  --size-selector: 0.25rem;
  --size-field: 0.25rem;

  /* Effects */
  --border: 1px;
  --depth: 1;
  --noise: 0;
}

.codx-primary {
  color: #cc0099;
}

.codx-secondary {
  color: #8f008f;
}

div[data-reka-popper-content-wrapper] {
  z-index: 2 !important;
}
```

---

## Design Rationale

| Dimension | Specification | Rationale |
|-----------|---------------|-----------|
| **Primary Color** | `oklch(58% 32 320)` | Converts #cc0099 to accessible, perceptually-even OKLch space. Maintains brand recognition while improving contrast. |
| **Secondary Color** | `oklch(42% 28 300)` | Darker magenta (#8f008f) creates visual hierarchy and supports multi-layer UI depth. |
| **Accent** | `oklch(65% 30 330)` | Slightly brighter than primary for call-to-action buttons—maintains family while drawing attention. |
| **Base/Content** | Light neutral backgrounds with minimal saturation | Ensures text legibility against magenta/purple without vibrating contrast. |
| **Semantic Colors** | Muted, purposeful hues | Success (green), Warning (amber), Error (red) follow WebAIM contrast standards. |
| **Border Radius** | Consistent 0.5–0.75rem scale | Modern, approachable feel without excessive roundness. Aligns with tech/dev tool aesthetics. |

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

❌ **Do NOT** use saturated magenta on dark backgrounds without sufficient lightness boost—causes eye strain.  
❌ **Do NOT** rely on color alone for semantic meaning (error/success)—always add icons or text labels.  
❌ **Do NOT** exceed 2 accent colors in UI—keeps cognitive load low and maintains professional polish.

---

## Next Steps

1. **Replace your `base.css`** with the theme code above.
2. **Test contrast** across buttons, links, and form inputs using WebAIM or Lighthouse.
3. **Share the sidebar component** so I can help you move the import/export actions inline with the Global Settings header.

Would you like me to refine the theme further or help with the sidebar restructuring?

