---

## 📋 Integration Steps

1. **Import in your main CSS file** (`base.css`):
   ```css client/src/assets/base.css
   @import "daisy-override.css";
   @import "tailwindcss";
   @plugin "@tailwindcss/typography";
   /* Remove the old daisyui plugin config */
   ```

2. **Update your Tailwind config** if needed to reference the new theme file in asset imports.

3. **Test theme switching** across all 33 themes to verify color consistency.

---

## ✅ What's Applied Across All Themes

| Property | codx-junior Value |
|----------|---|
| **Primary Color** | `#cc0099` (Magenta) |
| **Secondary Color** | `#8f008f` (Dark Magenta) |
| **Accent Color** | `#ff69b4` (Hot Pink) or theme-specific vibrant variant |

All other structural colors (base, info, success, warning, error) are preserved per theme to maintain visual hierarchy and semantic clarity while your brand colors dominate primary interactions.

---

## ⚠️ Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- **Don't override neutral/base colors with magenta** → Destroys readability of text & structure
- **Don't use codx colors at full saturation on dark bases** → Creates vibrating contrast; slightly desaturate (`#c41a8f` instead of `#cc0099`) for dark themes if needed
- **Don't apply the same accent to all themes** → Some themes (synthwave, acid, cyberpunk) have neon palettes; I've adjusted accents to harmonize

